// A function's NAME is a value only where a `fnptr` is wanted. Elsewhere it decayed to its C address, so this passed
// `kama check` and the C compiler refused it, or, for an argument, converted the address without a word. The fix is the
// call that was meant: `pi()`.
import { std::math::pi };
fn float32 take(float32 v) { return v; }
fn int32 main() { float32 a = 2.0f32; float32 x = pi; return 0; }
